PaddleOCR-Rust is an independent native-Rust port project. It is not an
official PaddlePaddle or PaddleOCR release and is not affiliated with or
endorsed by PaddlePaddle.

Project-authored source code, documentation, and self-authored fixtures are
made available under Apache License 2.0 as stated in LICENSE, unless a file
carries an explicit third-party notice.

References to PaddleOCR and PaddlePaddle identify the read-only upstream
behavioral reference used for compatibility research. No PaddleOCR source,
model weights, datasets, fonts, dictionaries, or third-party runtime artifacts
are included in this repository at the time of this notice.

Third-party behavioural references
----------------------------------

Several modules are independent Rust implementations whose observable behaviour
was derived by reading a third-party implementation. No third-party source is
copied into this repository. The attributions below are recorded because the
algorithms, their constants, and their edge-case behaviour were taken from those
implementations rather than independently invented.

OpenCV (Intel License Agreement / BSD 3-clause):

    Copyright (C) 2000, Intel Corporation, all rights reserved.
    Third party copyrights are property of their respective owners.

  src/contour.rs    modules/imgproc/src/contours.cpp
                    (icvFetchContour and the cvFindNextContour raster scan,
                    its direction table, marking rule, and contour ordering)
  src/min_area.rs   minAreaRect and boxPoints, including the corner order and
                    the non-strict tie comparison
  src/resize.rs     the INTER_LINEAR fixed-point resize, its coefficient bit
                    count, and its tap clamping
  src/crop.rs       warpPerspective with cubic sampling
  src/geometry.rs   the perspective transform setup and inverse mapping
  src/score.rs      the box-score edge walk and row fill
  src/image.rs      the imdecode colour, alpha, and bit-depth conventions

Clipper, via pyclipper (Boost Software License 1.0):

  src/unclip.rs     the polygon offset: JT_ROUND joins, ET_CLOSEDPOLYGON ends,
                    the miter limit, arc tolerance, and the truncation-toward-
                    zero coordinate ingest

PaddleOCR (Apache License 2.0) is the behavioural reference for the pipeline
itself: preprocessing order and constants, DB postprocessing sequence, batching
policy, CTC decoding, reading order, and result semantics. The pinned baseline
revision is recorded in ROADMAP.md and in every fixture's metadata. No PaddleOCR
source is copied into this repository.
